{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgVFabvU1MS9GdiaEggZw","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Receipts now go into the vault, and each claim keeps only the vault document id (`receipt_doc`). All 6 tests pass. The two new tests failed before the change.\n\n- **Storage:** `submit()` calls `vault.put()` with the receipt bytes. `receipt()` fetches the bytes from the vault.\n- **Retention:** The vault copy is stored for `RECEIPT_DAYS + 1` days. The vault purges on `stored + keep_days`, so the plain 60 would have hidden the receipt on day 60. Day 60 is still visible, and day 61 returns `None`. The vault itself now enforces the window, so a receipt is purged from storage rather than just hidden.\n- **Interface change:** `Claims` now takes an optional `vault` argument: `Claims(vault)`. With no argument it creates its own in-memory `Vault()`. In production you must pass the shared company vault. Otherwise receipts go into a private vault that is not the compliance-approved one. I made the argument optional so existing `Claims()` calls keep working. If you want a missing vault to be an error, say so.\n\n**Guesses:**\n- The 61-day vault keep time rests on my reading of \"60 days, day 60 included\". That is the same boundary guess as before.\n- I assumed the vault should purge the receipt at the end of the window. If compliance wants longer retention, change `keep_days`.\n\n**Not checked:**\n- This `Vault` is an in-memory class, so I can't tell whether it is compliance-approved storage in production.\n- I did not check any other callers of `Claims()`. This directory has none."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":798,"cache_read_input_tokens":42691,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":798},"output_tokens":524,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"stand